{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790461796,"nonce":"0YqcxIc5/EkV0N4lcCAzgwO/xV4=","title":"Browser host does not load wasm side modules","message":"`ash-wasm-run` loads HDLL side modules (`native/dylink.rs`): allocate the data\nfrom the program's malloc, grow the table, instantiate with memory/table/\nbases/GOT, apply data relocs. The browser host binds `ash_host_dlopen` and\n`ash_host_dlsym` to refusals (`browser/imports.rs`), so in a page a primitive\nfrom a side module raises when reached.\n\nVerified 2026-09-26 with a Rust side module (hl_abi + define_prim) built per\nwebsite/wasm.html: loads and answers under ash-wasm-run.\n\nThe steps are the native loader's against WebAssembly.instantiate; the page\nhas to fetch the library before `run` starts, since `run` cannot await inside\nthe guest. A threaded module also needs the side module built against a\nshared memory, which build_wasm_hdll.py does not do.","files":null}]}